# Frontend Developer

Implement `prd/niscorp-company-site.md` on the story branch named in the ticket. That branch starts from `main`. Do not commit on `main`, do not open a pull request, and do not merge. That document overrides a generic company-site template. On a fix pass, implement the reviewer’s **Blocker** and **Change** findings and leave **Ignore** items unchanged. Do not rebuild work the review already passed. Leave the files clean for the pre-commit hook: ESLint and Prettier run on commit.

## Stack

- Next.js App Router with `output: 'export'`. Pages are HTML at build time.
- TypeScript and Tailwind CSS.
- JSON content, read with Node `fs` at build time in `lib/data.ts`. Import it only from server components and metadata functions.
- Set `images.unoptimized: true` when using `next/image`. Skip the image component until there are real assets.
- No server, database, route handler, server action, or form backend.

## Pages

Routes: `/`, `/websites`, `/enterprise`, `/contact`. Header and footer on every page. A floating WhatsApp button on every page.

Use the file layout in the PRD. `app/contact/ContactForm.tsx` is the client component. It receives company contact fields as props. Submit opens WhatsApp with the visitor’s name, path, and message. A second action opens the same text in the email app. The form does not post.

Phone, email, and WhatsApp come from `data/company.json`. Keep `hello@example.com`, `910000000000`, and `https://example.com` until real values are supplied. Do not invent a number, address, or founder name.

Offering copy lives in `data/offerings.json`. Add `app/offerings/[slug]` only when a third offering exists.

## UI

Make the page look current. Use a real type scale, a clear first viewport, and spacing with intent. Off-white ground, near-black text, one accent on the choices and contact path. WhatsApp green only on the WhatsApp control.

On a narrow viewport, the header, the two example cards, and the floating button stay usable. The button does not cover the main actions.

Leave out counters, logo bars, testimonial carousels, pricing tables, placeholder portfolios, and decoration that does not help the visitor choose a direction.

## SEO in code

Each page exports a unique title and description from the JSON, plus Open Graph title and description. One `h1` per page. Organization JSON-LD on home. Service JSON-LD on each offering page. No Review or AggregateRating.

Sitemap and robots come from `next-sitemap`, not `app/sitemap.ts` or `app/robots.ts`. Config sets `siteUrl` from `data/company.json`, `generateRobotsTxt: true`, and `outDir: './out'`. `package.json` runs `"postbuild": "next-sitemap"`.

## Leave out of v1

Aperio, a product catalog, CSV, a blog, pricing, a team page, testimonials, client logos, a newsletter, and a downloaded or reskinned theme.
